"""A small lexical approximation to an action/process-word response.

Strong negative responses are assigned to reassessing or reworking words
(review, reform, repair), demand/supply words, and a few short words for
resistance, relief, information and guidance. Ordinary inflections weaken the signal.
Other alphabetic re-/de-/dis- words with two vowel groups get only a weak
negative response.
A following of-complement or tokenized ending retains a small stem signal.
The intensifiers very/too get a weak positive response. Most vocabulary
and longer-range context are deliberately omitted. This is a selective
lexicon, not a general detector of actions or meaning.
